message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Closure Cadence on S³: A Toy Model of Force Hierarchy from Quaternion Composition"
authors:
  - family-names: Guinan
    given-names: Leo
    affiliation: "MetaSPN / Proximity Fund"
  - family-names: da Silva
    given-names: Walter Henrique Alves
    affiliation: "Open Research Institute"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/leo-guinan/gut-driven-gut"
keywords:
  - force unification
  - quaternion dynamics
  - S3 geometry
  - toy model
  - closure
  - Hopf fibration
  - computational physics
abstract: >-
  A toy computational model exploring whether the four fundamental forces
  of physics arise from a single update mechanism operating at different
  energy scales. Cells on a lattice are unit quaternions updated by
  Hamilton product. Force-like behavior emerges from closure cadence —
  the rate at which running products return to identity on S³. Eight
  experiments with honest accounting: entropy conservation (CV=0.018),
  Hopf W/RGB shift with energy scale, qualitative force hierarchy and
  high-energy convergence. Failures documented: no confinement, no EM
  cancellation, 3 of 39 orders of magnitude.
